readme.text:
The provider reads `~/.cnb/token` (written by the official `cnb` CLI) and takes
`.auths["cnb.cool"].access_token`. The token is never printed or logged. A token lives ~8 hours:

- the file is re-read when its mtime/size changes, so a `cnb login` refresh is picked up without a restart;
- a 401 / `errcode: 16` response is reported as `unauthenticated` with a message telling the user to run
  `cnb login`;
- `CNB_TOKEN` can supply a token for one process instead of the file.

1. recovers the full repository-relative path from `blob_url`/`raw_url`/`contents_url`
   (`…/-/blob/{sha}/{path}`), never from `filename`;
2. emits per file: `diff --git a/<path> b/<path>`, `new file mode 100644`/`deleted file mode 100644`,
   `--- a/<path>` + `+++ b/<path>` (or `/dev/null` on the missing side), then the recorded hunks
   byte-for-byte, with LF line endings and a trailing newline;
3. renders an empty patch (`add`/`delete`/`modify`) as `Binary files … differ`, which jsdiff records as
   `isBinary`, instead of an empty change;
4. keeps rename origins when a payload exposes `previous_filename`; a CNB rename otherwise renders as a
   change of the new path.
